# Dockerfile.aio builds from the REPO ROOT, so web/.dockerignore and bff/.dockerignore do not apply here.
# Without this file, `COPY web/ ./` and `COPY bff/ ./` copy the host's node_modules straight over the ones
# `npm ci` just installed one layer earlier -- including native modules (sharp, @node-rs/argon2, mupdf)
# built for whatever the host happens to be. It also dragged ~790 MB of context into every build and
# defeated layer caching. CI never hit it because a fresh checkout has no node_modules.
**/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
bff/dist
.git
.env
docker-compose.override.yml
# The desktop app (Electron shell, bundled Postgres, engine packs) is never part of an image. Its staged
# resources/ and dist/ run to hundreds of MB on a machine that has built it, and all of that would otherwise
# be sent as build context on every `docker build .`. desktop-engine/ was the Phase 0 spike's folder; listed so
# an old checkout that still has one does not send it either.
desktop/
desktop-engine/
prebuilt/
